[ ] Project shared workspace state into Neovim =nvim-projection $Create a thin human projection using native quickfix, signs, commands, statusline data, and semantic jumps. Start with quickfix plus explicit status/delta commands; add latency-sensitive signs/statusline/jumps only against bounded kernel projections. The shared substrate is authoritative; Neovim remains the human cockpit rather than the daemon.$ !3 +integration ^2026-08-31T22:31 <orientation-hardening #01a05b73-6884-79b2-a3af-4577cc07e03a
[ ] Fix Pi Lens stale diagnostic cache and disposition handling =pi-lens-stale-cache $Pi Lens continued reporting four impossible Pyright findings for .claude/hooks/orient-session.py after the source was fixed: line 131/154 findings on a 130-line file, duplicate main when only one declaration exists, and removed preview_index. python3 -m py_compile and the 16-check hook drive pass. Repeated lsp/full refreshes stayed stale, and exact false-positive dispositions (including reanchored lines/rules) did not remove the blocking mode=all cache entries. Reproduce and fix cache invalidation/disposition matching so stale intermediate-edit diagnostics cannot remain blocking.$ !5 +environment ^2026-09-02T11:13 #01a06353-172a-7240-97ea-ac52d873eec1
[-] Foreign dogfood\: earn trust under real stakes =foreign-dogfood $Move Agent Workspace beyond recursive self-dogfood by running a real multi-session task in a foreign repository and measuring behavioral reliance, not merely correct output. Accepted architecture: install the kernel independently of target repositories; keep dynamic logs, payloads, checkpoints, and live transactions in external XDG-style local state; partition one logical project workspace by workstream, worktree, actor, and session; keep working sets session-local and transaction state worktree-local; do not infer shared identity across clones from remote URL alone. A small optional locator/policy manifest and explicit reconciled checkpoint export may travel later, but dynamic state does not travel implicitly with Git. Clearhead remains authoritative for what work exists, priority, predecessors, and lifecycle; Agent Workspace owns epistemic execution state. Workspace Objective is an objective binding to Clearhead, another tracker, or an ad hoc user intent, not a duplicate task record. First slice: installed-kernel discovery, external project registry/state, global Pi projection, and attribution. Then perform a genuine handoff where a cold agent consumes automatic status/delta, reuses at least one narrow current claim without rereading, re-observes an unseen stale dependency before acting, and records false-current, false-stale, bypass, bookkeeping, latency, and context-cost evidence. See docs/decision-external-workspace-and-clearhead-boundary.md.$ !2 +evaluation ^2026-09-02T16:15 #01a06468-1bb3-7ee2-81fb-a8378951f125
[ ] Modularize the kernel\: split the core impls =modularize-kernel $Continue the lib.rs modularization begun 2026-09-02 (model/projection/reconcile extracted; lib.rs 4380->2595). Remaining bulk is impl Workspace (command methods) and impl Projection (reducer). Splitting them requires a design decision FIRST: making Workspace and Projection private fields pub(crate) so methods in other modules can reach them. That decision is the gate and the reason this is its own action, not a drive-by. Behavior-preserving; tests stay green. NOTE: ~2500-line lib.rs is fine for agents (grep+offset), so this is optional cleanup pulled by human review, not an agent need.$ !6 +implementation ^2026-09-02T16:15 #01a06468-1bc2-7340-8a3e-d7f06319162f
[ ] pi-mcp-client =pi-mcp-client $Refactor .pi/extensions/agent-workspace/ from a parallel native-tool server into a thin MCP client + capture hook, per docs/decision-mcp-centered-tool-surface.md. PRECONDITIONS MET 2026-09-04 (commit 7314b40): the mcp server carries the full write loop (record_belief, bind_objective, supersede_claim, checkpoint, observe_read). SLICE ORDER: (A) FIRST add the five read-surface verbs to src/mcp.rs — workspace_status (resume_brief_status/resume_status on full), workspace_delta (delta_brief_since/delta_since, since param), workspace_working_set, workspace_findings, workspace_transaction_preview (resume_transaction_preview; map None to TransactionNotFound-style error) — the extension exposes these five today and registering only discovered MCP tools would regress the surface. Note: CLI --compact is only single-line vs pretty JSON, irrelevant over MCP. (B) THEN refactor the extension: dep @modelcontextprotocol/sdk ^1.30.0 (USER DECISION: official SDK, no hand-rolled client); spawn agent-workspace mcp --repository <root> via StdioClientTransport, one Client per repo root, lazy connect, session_shutdown closes clients (event exists in Pi). Pi ExtensionFactory supports async (void|Promise<void>) so discovery-at-load is possible, but the factory gets no cwd ctx — resolve via process.cwd() or keep per-execute resolution; that is the one open design point. Pi providers consume tool parameters as plain JSON Schema (schema.properties/required; NO TypeBox Value.Check in runtime path — verified in pi-ai dist/api/anthropic-messages.js convertTools) so MCP inputSchema passes through with a cast. promptSnippet/promptGuidelines/label are Pi-specific metadata absent from MCP: keep a small static Pi-metadata map keyed by tool name with fallbacks. Capture hook routes to the client's workspace_observe_read instead of observe-read CLI stdin; model_visible_bytes accounting must survive the JSON hop (test asserts today). tests/mcp_stdio.rs is the proven reference wire client (newline-delimited JSON-RPC). Step 4 (deprecate TS native tools) stays gated on parity evidence; live-confirm in a RESTARTED Claude Code session after. Acceptance: all current Pi tests green against the MCP path, no tool lost vs today's six, capture byte accounting preserved, absence-of-runtime degrades harmlessly.$ !2 +integration ^2026-09-05T00:33 <01a06f11 #01a0707c-282c-7471-a29e-719e4636b805
